# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0019027> (otopalatodigital syndrome)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "Orphanet:669") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0019027> "A form of frontootopalatodigital syndrome, characterized by deafness, cleft palate, and characteristic digital anomalies. OPD syndrome is divided into two forms based on severity: the milder form designated OPD type 1 (OPD1), and the more severe and often lethal form designated OPD type 2 (OPD2). OPD is an X-linked disorder. Two other genetic disorders with features overlapping OPD, frontometaphyseal dysplasia (FMD) and osteodysplasty, Melnick-Needles type (MNS) have been described; thus OPD1, OPD2, FMD, and MNS are allelic disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "MONDO:GARD") <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0019027> "GARD:0007293")
