AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0019269> "Epidermal keratinocytes undergo a unique form of terminal differentiation and programmed cell death known as cornification. Cornification leads to the formation of the outermost skin barrier, i.e. the cornified layer, as well as to the formation of hair and nails. (PMID:23792051)")
