# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0019270> (erythrokeratoderma)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://rarediseases.org/rare-diseases/https-rarediseases-org-rare-diseases-erythrokeratoderma/") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0019270> "An umbrella term for a group of rare genetic skin disorders characterized by well-demarcated plaques of reddened, dry and thickened skin. Typically, these lesions are distributed symmetrically on the body and tend to slowly expand and progress over time.")
