# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0019330> (pili gemini)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "Orphanet:79492") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0019330> "Pili gemini defines a situation where the papilla's tip of a hair follicle splits during the anagen phase and consequently grows two hair shafts emerging through a single pilary canal. A papilla tip that divides in several tips will produce several hair shafts, a situation named pili multigemini. Pili gemini or multigemini can occur in each type of hair.")
