# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0019800> (obsolete chronic hepatic porphyria)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "Orphanet:95161") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0019800> "OBSOLETE. Chronic hepatic porphyrias represent a sub-group of porphyrias. They are characterized by bullous photodermatitis caused by a deficiency of uroporphyrinogen decarboxylase (URO-D; the fifth enzyme in the heme biosynthesis pathway). Chronic hepatic porphyria encompasses two diseases: porphyria cutanea tarda and hepatoerythropoietic porphyria (extremely rare).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "MONDO:excludeGrouping") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000231> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0019800> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0001000>)
